      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence supports a partial hypothesis. The Discussion section explains the divergence between Twitter and web data, attributing Twitter's representation to wealthier populations (matching GDP-weighted populations better, internet-usage worse) and to the urban-centered collection. It also notes fewer missing languages in Twitter and that Twitter has more false positives (indicating more diverse language populations). Together this offers a hypothesis rationale for why Twitter may capture the language inventory better. The evidence directly addresses the question, so answer is appropriate."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 4696.348799974658
    },
